/* THE CORPUS, AS CHUNKS. `obs` is the OBSERVATION DATE - when the fact is asserted about,
   not when the document was filed. `kind` is what the chunk physically is; it is the second
   half of the WBC defect, because a lab table chunks into rows that are numerically dense and
   semantically thin while a sentence naming the same value is neither.
   `sim` is the seeded cosine similarity WHEN THE CHUNK IS ON SUBJECT. `off` is what it scores
   when it is not - kept explicit so the eligibility floor has something real to exclude. */
